# @podlite/diagram

=head1 Upcoming

=item React 19 is accepted as a peer: C<react> and C<react-dom> are C<^16.0.0 || ^17.0.0 || ^18 || ^19>

=item the diagram component names its return type, so its declaration reads the same with the types of React 16 to 19

=item C<react-is> is no longer a dependency or a peer: the package does not load it

=head1 0.0.86

=item C<mermaid> 11.16.1 or later is required, and only as a dependency of the package: version 11.16.1 fixes prototype pollution, CSS injection and loops on crafted diagrams, and an application can no longer supply an older C<mermaid> in its place. The lock file of the monorepo resolves C<dompurify> under C<mermaid> to 3.4.17; an application with its own lock file keeps the version it has until it updates it

=head1 0.0.75

=item a hidden diagram shows its source masked and is not drawn, so the drawing cannot show what it hides; its caption is masked too

=head1 0.0.74

=item the package can be imported from Node directly. The emitted ESM referenced its own files without an extension, which the ESM loader refuses


=head1 0.0.56

=item upgrade mermaid to 11 (async render API), fixing known security advisories

=head1 0.0.52

=item add C<exports> map, top-level C<types>, and explicit C<sideEffects> to package manifest

=head1 0.0.50

=item fix C<=Mermaid> crash on empty block content

=head1 0.0.23

=item fix react component

=head1 0.0.20

